│ Mode 2:                                                                      │
│ x1[1\] = x2[0\]                                                              │
│ x2[1\] = a2*x1[0\] + b2*x2[0\] + c2                                          │
│                                                                              │
│ 1. Load the data.                                                            │
│ 2. Estimate derivatives dx1/dt and dx2/dt using a high-order method (e.g.,   │
│ 5-point stencil) given dt=0.001.                                             │
│ 3. Locate the switching point accurately. It's around x1 = -0.4955. Use the  │
│ change in dynamics of x2[1\] to find the exact index.                        │
